# Strategy Validation Gates

- This repository uses validation gates as evidence requirements inside the existing status machine, not as a parallel state system. Status labels remain defined only in `docs/research-governance/strategy-status-glossary.md`.
- Gate details, default thresholds, report expectations, and allowed deviations live in `docs/research-governance/strategy-validation-gates.md`. Do not copy the full checklist into core ledgers, README routing tables, or AGENTS.md.
- Registration/freeze and promotion are distinct operations: `explore -> registered` fixes version identity and evidence links only. “登记/冻结 Vx” never means “promote Vx”.
- At registration, record known gate gaps without automatically running the full review.
- Before `dry-run -> live`, complete one promotion review covering all hard gates (excess-return baseline, ablation, OOS/CPCV, Monte Carlo robustness, stress tests) and the existing live-executable audit. Missing or failed hard-gate evidence keeps the version at `dry-run / not live-ready`, or at `registered / not promoted / not live-ready` if it never entered dry-run. `registered -> live spec` and `registered -> dry-run` only require frozen identity, a runner-reproducible spec, complete handoff-spec fields, and (for dry-run) `runner-tracking/`.
- Phase/bar-alignment sensitivity is a non-mandatory check item, not a hard gate. Run and report it when suitable finer-grained data are available; poor phase performance, a missed reference line, or unavailable phase data cannot alone block promotion. If the check exposes lookahead, invalid aggregation, unavailable source data, or runner parity failure, apply the corresponding hard gate instead.
- Statistical significance (PSR/DSR/MinTRL) and start-time sensitivity are optional diagnostics. Phase/bar-alignment is a report-only check item when feasible. None of these is a hard blocker. Historical reports that scored old gates 5/6/7 keep their contemporaneous numbering.
- `registered -> dry-run` may skip `live spec`. `live spec -> dry-run -> live` remains governed by the runner handoff, runner-tracking, and operations rules in `lab-runner-handoff.mdc` and `live-executable-strategy-research.mdc`. `dry-run -> live` additionally requires a completed online open/close reconciliation report comparing runtime fills against backtest expectations (see `lab-runner-handoff.mdc`); offline parity alone is insufficient. Live-executable audit and hard gates are required before `live`, not before `dry-run`.
- Gate thresholds are default repository standards, not immutable constants. A report may use a stricter or different threshold only when it states why the default is unsuitable, what replacement was used, and records the deviation in the family `decision-log.md`.
- Do not treat unavailable data as a pass. Missing data for a hard gate remains an incomplete blocker; missing finer-grained data for the phase check is recorded as `not checked / insufficient data` without independently blocking promotion.
- Gate evidence belongs under the relevant family directory: durable Markdown in `diagnostics/`, `ablations/`, or `notes/` by nature; scripts in `scripts/`; retained JSON/CSV/plots in `artifacts/`; state changes in `decision-log.md`; compact links and status in the core ledger.
- Existing dry-run or historical versions are not automatically downgraded by this rule. Apply these gates to new promotion attempts and to any later attempt to move an existing version toward `live`.
